Script 1 What Does Hypnosis Actually Do to Your Brain\
Most people think hypnosis is something that happens to you. A watch swinging. A snap of the fingers. Lights out.\
That is not what hypnosis is. Not even close.\
What hypnosis actually does is move your brain into a specific state. A natural state. One that your brain already knows how to reach on its own. It just gets there deliberately instead of by accident.\
Your brain operates at different frequencies depending on what you are doing. When you are stressed and overthinking, that is one frequency. When you are calm and drifting, that is another. When you are in deep dreamless sleep, that is another still.\
Hypnosis works by guiding your brain into the frequencies where it is most open to change. Where the critical, analytical, skeptical part of your mind quiets down. And where something deeper becomes accessible.\
Not unconscious. Not asleep. Not under anyone's control.\
Just open. Focused. And ready to do the work that normal waking life makes almost impossible.\
Everything you think you know about hypnosis probably came from a TV show or a stage act. The reality is far more interesting. And far more useful. Follow for more.\
