\cf0 Script 2 The 5 Brain Wave States Explained Simply\
Your brain is always producing electrical activity. And depending on what you are doing, that activity runs at different speeds. These speeds are called brain wave states. And there are five of them.\
The first is gamma. This is your brain at peak performance. Heightened perception. Flow state. The feeling of being completely locked in.\
The second is beta. This is normal waking consciousness. Active thinking. Analysis. Problem solving. Most of us live here almost all day.\
The third is alpha. This is where things start to get interesting. Calm. Relaxed. Eyes closed. This is the gateway into deeper states.\
The fourth is theta. Deep relaxation. Creativity. Daydreaming. This is where hypnosis lives. This is where real change becomes possible.\
The fifth is delta. Deep dreamless sleep. The unconscious mind at rest.\
Most people only know about two of these states, awake and asleep. But there is a whole spectrum in between. And learning to access the states in the middle is one of the most powerful things you can do for your mind. Follow for more.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Script 3 What Gamma Waves Are and When You Experience Them\
You know that feeling when everything just clicks?\
When you are so locked into what you are doing that time disappears. Your thinking is sharp. Your perception is heightened. Everything feels connected. You are not trying. You are just flowing.\
That is gamma.\
Gamma is the fastest brain wave state. Running between 30 and 100 cycles per second. It is associated with peak focus, heightened awareness, and what psychologists call flow state.\
Athletes feel it in the middle of a perfect game. Musicians feel it when a performance takes on a life of its own. Writers feel it when the words come faster than they can type.\
It is not something you can force. Trying to get into gamma usually pushes you further away from it. It tends to emerge when you are deeply engaged, highly skilled at something, and fully present.\
Most people experience gamma in short bursts without even realizing what it is. The more you understand your brain states, the more you can create the conditions for it to happen. Follow for more.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Script 4 What Beta Waves Are and Why Most of Us Are Stuck There\
Here is an uncomfortable truth about modern life.\
Most of us spend almost our entire waking day in a single brain state. Beta. And it is slowly exhausting us.\
Beta is normal waking consciousness. Active thinking. Analysis. Decision making. Problem solving. It runs at 12 to 30 cycles per second and it is the state your brain defaults to the moment your alarm goes off in the morning.\
Beta is useful. You need it to function. But the problem is that most people never leave it.\
Constant stimulation. Screens. Notifications. Deadlines. The relentless inner monologue of a mind that never gets to rest. All of it keeps the brain locked in beta all day long.\
And a brain that never gets to slow down never gets to recover. Never gets to process. Never gets to access the deeper, quieter states where creativity lives, where healing happens, where real insight becomes possible.\
The goal is not to eliminate beta. It is to stop being trapped there. To learn how to shift states deliberately. So that your brain gets the full range of what it is capable of. Follow for more.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Script 5 What Alpha Waves Are and Why They Matter\
There is a brain state that most people stumble into by accident. But almost nobody uses on purpose. And it might be the most valuable state your brain can be in.\
It is called alpha.\
Alpha runs at 8 to 12 cycles per second. It is the state of calm relaxed awareness. Eyes closed. Body still. Mind quiet but not asleep. It is what your brain does naturally when you sit in the sun and let your thoughts drift. When you take a long shower and ideas suddenly start flowing. When you finally stop doing and just breathe.\
Alpha is called the gateway state. Because it sits right between the busy analytical beta state and the deep transformative theta state. It is the bridge.\
When you are in alpha, the critical analytical part of your mind starts to relax. The inner voice that constantly evaluates and judges and second guesses begins to quiet down.\
And in that quiet, something becomes possible that is almost impossible in normal waking life. You become genuinely open. To new ideas. To new feelings. To new beliefs about yourself.\
This is why meditation works. Why breathwork works. Why hypnosis works. They all lead to the same place. Alpha. And what waits just beyond it. Follow for more.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Script 6 What Theta Waves Are and Why They Are So Powerful\
If alpha is the gateway, theta is what is on the other side of the door.\
Theta brain waves run at 4 to 8 cycles per second. This is the state of deep relaxation, hypnosis, vivid creativity, and daydreaming. It is where your brain goes in the moments just before you fall asleep. And in the hazy moments just after you wake up.\
In theta, the conscious analytical mind steps aside. And the deeper parts of your mind, the parts that hold your beliefs, your memories, your emotional responses, your ingrained patterns of behavior, become accessible in a way they simply are not in normal waking consciousness.\
This is why theta is so significant for change work.\
Most of the patterns people want to change, the fears, the limiting beliefs, the automatic reactions that seem to have a life of their own, were formed and are stored below the level of conscious thought. You cannot reach them by thinking harder. You cannot reason your way to them.\
But in theta, you can.\
The brain in theta is not passive. It is deeply receptive. Focused inward. And extraordinarily open to new information, new associations, and new ways of seeing itself.\
This is not mystical. It is neuroscience. Follow for more.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Script 7 What Delta Waves Are and What Happens in Them\
Delta is the deepest brain state of all. And it is the one you visit every single night without even trying.\
Delta waves run at the slowest frequency of all five states, between half a cycle and 4 cycles per second. This is the state of deep dreamless sleep. The body in full repair mode. The conscious mind completely offline.\
In delta you are not dreaming. You are not processing the day. You are not thinking at all in any meaningful sense. The brain has essentially turned off all non essential activity so the body can do the work of healing, restoring and rebuilding.\
Growth hormone is released in delta. The immune system does its most significant work in delta. Memory consolidation, the process of moving information from short term to long term storage, happens partly in delta.\
Most people do not think much about delta because they are unconscious when it is happening. But the quality of your delta sleep affects almost everything about how you feel and function when you wake up.\
Poor delta sleep means poor recovery. Poor recovery means a brain and body that are constantly running on less than they need. Which makes everything harder. The mood. The focus. The resilience. The ability to handle stress.\
You cannot access delta consciously. But you can create the conditions for it. And that starts with understanding the states that lead you there. Follow for more.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
