\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Script 8 Why Hypnosis Is Not Sleep and Not Unconsciousness\
Almost every misconception about hypnosis comes from the same mistake. People think it is a form of unconsciousness. That you go under. That you are not in control. That someone else takes the wheel.\
None of that is true.\
In hypnosis your brain is not in delta, the deep sleep state. It is not even in the drowsy edges of sleep. It is in alpha and theta. Which are active, aware, focused states.\
You can hear everything. You are aware of your surroundings. You can choose to open your eyes and walk out of the room at any moment. Your critical mind has not been switched off. It has simply been quieted enough to allow a deeper level of the mind to become accessible.\
Think of it like this. Imagine your conscious analytical mind is a loud radio playing in a busy room. In normal waking consciousness that radio is turned all the way up. It is hard to hear anything else over it. In hypnosis the volume gets turned down. The radio is still there. You can still hear it if you focus on it. But now you can also hear the quieter things underneath it. The things that are usually drowned out.\
That is hypnosis. Not unconsciousness. Not sleep. Not surrender. A deliberate, focused, deeply aware state. One that you already know how to reach. You just have not been doing it on purpose. Follow for more.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
